1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Every line of this invoice is right.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
The total is one cent off. Every test passes.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:20,000
This is how old business software dies: someone rewrites it,
nobody can say what the old one really did,

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
and the bugs that slip through are business bugs. Parity rebuilds the app
and proves the new one does the same thing, field by field.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
You record someone using the old app and talking.
Muse Voice Transcribe reads the narration,

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Muse Spark and SAM read every field on every key frame,
and the business rules come out in plain language, each with its evidence.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The formulas are checked against the recorded values by code.
An expert accepts them in a click.

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Muse Code builds the web app from the accepted rules.
Parity replays the same invoice on it:

9
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:15,000
eight of eight fields equal, first try, forty-six cents.

10
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:25,000
And when a rebuild adds the rounded taxes instead of rounding once,
Parity names the field: 69.21 before, 69.22 after.

11
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:35,000
AI never decides what the same means. The comparison is plain code.

12
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:45,000
On an app nobody here wrote, FrontAccounting,
Parity fuzzes the rebuild against the live app.

13
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:55,000
It found three items the recording never showed, shrank each
to a one-line invoice, and one repair closed them.

14
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:05,000
The proof stays. Every pull request is replayed by a GitHub Action, with no model call;
a change that breaks the cent fails its check.

15
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:15,000
And a coding agent can call Parity itself, through MCP,
before it opens its pull request.

16
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Muse Spark computer use explores the app alone, confined to it,
and turns the screens nobody recorded into tests.

17
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Migration mode goes screen by screen: customers, items and invoices,
on records read through the old app's own forms, each one proved.

18
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Nothing leaves your machine unless you send it.
Cut the network: the proof still runs.

19
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Every model call is in the send log, with its cost.
The whole hackathon cost eighteen dollars.

20
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Parity. Record it once, prove it forever. Open source.
